@api @pdf @smoke
Feature: PDF content validation

  Verifies the content of generated PDFs (invoices, statements, reports) via utils.PdfUtil
  (Apache PDFBox) — text, page count, and metadata. The PDF is generated by the Given step itself
  (steps.PdfSteps), since no real invoicing feature exists in this framework yet; point the same
  Then steps at a real generated PDF's path once one does.

  Scenario: A generated invoice PDF's text and metadata can be validated
    Given a sample PDF "invoice-1001.pdf" is generated with title "Invoice #1001" and author "Billing System" containing:
      | Invoice #1001      |
      | Customer: Jane Doe |
      | Total Due: $249.99 |
    Then the PDF should have 1 page
    And the PDF text should contain "Invoice #1001"
    And the PDF text should contain "Total Due: $249.99"
    And the PDF metadata title should be "Invoice #1001"
    And the PDF metadata author should be "Billing System"
    And the PDF is attached to the Allure report

  Scenario: A multi-page report PDF's page count can be validated
    Given a sample PDF "report-2026-q1.pdf" is generated with 3 pages each containing the text "Quarterly Report"
    Then the PDF should have 3 pages
    And the PDF text should contain "Quarterly Report (page 2)"
